\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For fixed $0<\kappa <8$, put $d=1+\kappa /8$ and $h(r)=r^d(\log $ $\log (1/r))^((2-d)/2)$ near zero. Does ordinary chordal $SLE_\kappa $ have positive finite h-Hausdorff measure on every positive-time compact trace segment on one probability-one event, and finite expected h-measure of its entire trace in each deterministic bounded ball?

\subsection{Short English statement}
